## Context

`scripts/skill-doctor-survey.py` has 7 clusterers and ~400 lines but no
test coverage. The survey was validated manually against live data, but
regressions (e.g., the hardcoded frequency floor in `_cluster_ticket_line_format`
that was caught during review) would go undetected.

## Actions

1. Add `tests/test_skill_doctor_survey.py` with unit tests for:
   - `_cluster_budget_raises`: deduplication of git commits by message
   - `_cluster_dirty_tree`: pattern matching on French/English error messages
   - `_cluster_watermark_redetection`: keyword matching in journal entries
   - `_cluster_umbrella_not_closed`: journal + log line merging
   - `_cluster_ticket_line_format`: real frequency (no hardcoded floor)
   - `_cluster_max_turns`: journal + log merging
   - `_cluster_crash_recovery`: threshold filtering
   - `_resolve_harness_dir`: worktree path resolution

2. Test edge cases:
   - Empty inputs (no journal, no logs, no commits)
   - Below-threshold frequencies (should return None)
   - `--min-frequency` filtering

## Exit criteria

- `pytest tests/test_skill_doctor_survey.py` passes
- Each clusterer has at least one positive and one below-threshold test
- `_resolve_harness_dir` tested with mocked `.git` file
